{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Firepans.</b> With them they scoop embers for the terumah of the ash, which is made like a pan that has only three walls, and with its front side it draws the embers." "<b>Forks.</b> Bronze implements with which they strike the limbs on the altar to turn them, so that they burn well and quickly." "<b>Basins.</b> They are shovels — וודי״ל בְּלַעַ״ז — of bronze, and with them they clear the ash from upon the altar."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French *vadille* (a type of shovel/basket)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:21.703942447Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}